title: Drill — record, count, play
chapter: 21
type: drill
skills: macro-record, macro-count
par: 44
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: six cursors and two rounds of typing
open: refund.spec.ts

@brief
Six bare calls in a test need wrapping:

    isRefundable(recentOrder)    →    expect(isRefundable(recentOrder)).toBe(true);

Record on the first, count the rest. Eight times, until `qa` and `q`
stop being decisions.

@keys
| `qa` … `q` | record |
| `5@a` | play five times |
| `^` `A` | start of line, append at the end |

@hints
`^iexpect(` and `Esc`, `A).toBe(true);` and `Esc`, `j`. That is the
whole recording.
--
Two lines down to the first call, record, then `5@a`. Do not count the
lines on the screen; you know there are six.

@solution
    2j  qa ^iexpect( <Esc> A).toBe(true); <Esc> j q   5@a   :wq<Enter>

Thirty-six keystrokes. The aim of the drill is the shape: position,
`qa`, edit, `j`, `q`, count, `@a`. When that is one motion in your
hands you stop thinking about macros as a feature and start reaching
for them the moment you see the second identical line.

@start refund.spec.ts
describe('isRefundable', () => {
  it('accepts orders inside the window', () => {
    isRefundable(recentOrder)
    isRefundable(paidOrder)
    isRefundable(packedOrder)
    isRefundable(shippedOrder)
    isRefundable(deliveredOrder)
    isRefundable(giftOrder)
  });
});

@expected refund.spec.ts
describe('isRefundable', () => {
  it('accepts orders inside the window', () => {
    expect(isRefundable(recentOrder)).toBe(true);
    expect(isRefundable(paidOrder)).toBe(true);
    expect(isRefundable(packedOrder)).toBe(true);
    expect(isRefundable(shippedOrder)).toBe(true);
    expect(isRefundable(deliveredOrder)).toBe(true);
    expect(isRefundable(giftOrder)).toBe(true);
  });
});
